<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
        <RootNamespace>Bennewitz.Ninja.AgentForge.Artifacts</RootNamespace>
        <AssemblyName>AgentForge.Artifacts</AssemblyName>
        <Description>
            Artifact resolution: where agents, commands, skills, rules and memory files come
            from, and which definition of a given name actually applies.

            The model is an ordered list of SOURCES rather than a hardcoded directory walk.
            That is the whole point: Claude reads a fixed set of locations, while OpenCode
            traverses upward to the git worktree root, reads three separate skill roots, and
            accepts the same artifact declared both as a markdown file and as inline JSON. A
            walk cannot express that; an ordered source list can, and Claude becomes the
            degenerate case of one.

            Resolution GROUPS AND ORDERS; it does not merge. Per name it returns the whole
            chain, highest precedence first, mirroring LayeredValue/ScopeEntry so the existing
            scope-badge UI binds with no new controls. How a chain collapses to one effective
            artifact is per-kind policy and deliberately lives outside this type — Spike S7
            measured that OpenCode's inline JSON and markdown DEEP-MERGE with the file winning
            per field, so a resolver that picked one winner and discarded the rest would be
            structurally unable to express the truth.

            Framework-only by design: no package references, and no knowledge of any product's
            paths. A source supplies its own entries; this assembly never touches PlatformPaths.

            Invariant: AgentForge.* must never reference ClaudeForge.* or OpenCode.*.
            AssemblyLayeringTests enforces it.
        </Description>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="AgentForge.Artifacts.Tests"/>
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
